# Winning a travel fight with no journey under it returns to the world view.
#
# The sibling of fight_victory_travel_arrival.cli, reached from the other end: --start-fight drops
# into a fight on arrival at the world map, so there is no path in flight at all. The victory branch
# used to resume travel unconditionally, which parked the game in Traveling with no path to walk and
# no travel box even drawn — a black screen.
#
# Both cases are the same mistake ("victory means carry on walking"), and both are asserted because
# the fix has two arms: deliver a held arrival, else fall back to the world view.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --start-fight wolf

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue

# --start-fight fires on arrival at the world map, before the view becomes interactive.
wait mode Fighting 90

fight-end victory

wait mode WorldView 60
# Idle, not merely in the right mode: a stranded Traveling never settles either, and `state` reports
# the mode of a game that has stopped answering exactly as it reports a working one.
wait 30

quit
